{
 "brief": "Widespread anger erupted in Gaza after the Fatah movement converted higher education institutions into political venues, Shehab Wire reported. Palestine University hosted the movement's Revolutionary Council meeting, while Al-Azhar University served as the site for Fatah's eighth conference, drawing sharp criticism from residents and observers who objected to the use of academic facilities for partisan purposes.\n\nThe conversions sparked discontent over what critics characterized as the politicization of universities and their diversion from educational missions to advance party interests. The incidents raised concerns about the autonomy of Gaza's higher education sector and its ability to function independently from political factions.",
